---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Order two transactions" hint="Transaction T1 commits through one coordinator. A client then starts T2 at another coordinator whose clock is a little different. Choose how uncertain TrueTime is, how far apart the two clocks really are, and whether the commit waits, and see whether T2 is correctly ordered after T1. A simple model with round numbers, not Google's code or data.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>. On <b>A quiet day</b>, with clocks that are <b>Close together</b>, a write takes <b>10</b> ms: the commit wait of <b>8</b> ms is hidden inside the Paxos commit. T1 gets timestamp <b>7</b> and T2 gets <b>11</b>, so T2 is correctly ordered after T1, by a margin of <b>4</b> ms.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Uncertainty</b> to <b>A TrueTime spike</b>. Twice the uncertainty is now <b>24</b> ms, longer than the Paxos commit, so every write takes <b>24</b> ms instead of 10. The order is still right: T1 gets <b>15</b> and T2 gets <b>33</b>, a margin of <b>18</b> ms.</li>
    <li>Now set <b>Clocks</b> to <b>Far apart</b> and <b>Commit wait</b> to <b>Skip the wait</b>. Writes are quick again, at <b>10</b> ms, but the clocks differ by <b>20</b> ms and nothing makes T2 wait: T1 gets <b>22</b> and T2 gets only <b>12</b>, so T2 is ordered <b>10</b> ms before a transaction that had already committed.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Commit wait</b> to <b>Wait until the timestamp has passed</b>. Writes cost <b>24</b> ms again, and the order is restored: T1 gets <b>22</b>, T2 gets <b>26</b>, and the margin is <b>4</b> ms in T2's favour.</li>
    <li>Finally set <b>Clocks</b> to <b>Beyond the bound</b>. The clocks now differ by <b>30</b> ms, more than twice the 12 ms of uncertainty that TrueTime claimed, so its bound was not honest. Even with the wait, T1 gets <b>27</b> and T2 only <b>21</b>, out of order by <b>6</b> ms. The wait protects only as far as the bound is true.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg spt" data-spt>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Uncertainty <select class="pg-in" data-uncertainty><option value="4">A quiet day</option><option value="12">A TrueTime spike</option></select></label>
      <label>Clocks <select class="pg-in" data-gap><option value="6">Close together</option><option value="20">Far apart</option><option value="30">Beyond the bound</option></select></label>
      <label>Commit wait <select class="pg-in" data-wait><option value="on">Wait until the timestamp has passed</option><option value="off">Skip the wait</option></select></label>
      <button type="button" class="btn" data-reset>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Time to commit a write</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Commit wait</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>T2 compared with T1</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Is TrueTime's bound honest?</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <svg class="spt-chart" viewBox="0 0 600 130" role="img" data-chart preserveAspectRatio="none">
      <line data-axis x1="20" x2="580" y1="65" y2="65" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1" />
      <circle data-t1 r="9" fill="var(--role-1)" />
      <circle data-t2 r="9" fill="var(--role-3)" />
      <text data-t1-label font-size="14" fill="var(--text)" text-anchor="middle">T1</text>
      <text data-t2-label font-size="14" fill="var(--text)" text-anchor="middle">T2</text>
    </svg>
    <p class="pg-note">The commit timestamps on a time line (earlier to the left). T2 should always be to the right of T1, because T2 started after T1 had committed.</p>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model, invented for teaching and not Google data. The choices mean: on a quiet day TrueTime's uncertainty is 4 ms and in a spike it is 12 ms; the two clocks are 6 ms apart when close together, 20 ms when far apart and 30 ms when beyond the bound. T1 reaches its coordinator, whose clock runs ahead of true time by half the gap. A client then starts T2 at once, at a coordinator whose clock runs behind by half the gap. Each coordinator takes the latest end of its TrueTime interval, its clock plus the uncertainty, as its commit timestamp. The Paxos commit takes 10 ms. With commit wait, a write is acknowledged when both the Paxos commit and a wait of twice the uncertainty have finished, whichever is later. Without it, as soon as Paxos is done. The paper says the expected commit wait is at least twice the average uncertainty and is typically overlapped with Paxos, and in its one-replica measurements a write took 10.1 ms without commit wait and 14.1 ms with it. Real systems are more complicated than this.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<style>
  .spt-chart { width: 100%; height: 130px; display: block; background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; }
</style>
<script>
  import { query } from '../../playground';
  import { simulate } from '../../models/spanner-time.ts';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-spt]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const PAXOS_MS = 10; // the paper's one-replica Paxos latency
    const CHART_LEFT = 40, CHART_RIGHT = 560, CHART_Y = 65, LABEL_OFFSET = 4;
    const CHART_MIN_MS = 0, CHART_MAX_MS = 40; // the time line runs from 0 to 40 ms after T1 reached its coordinator
    const DEFAULTS: Record<string, string> = { uncertainty: '4', gap: '6', wait: 'on' };
    const select = (key: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(`[data-${key}]`);
    const ms = (n: number) => `${n} ms`;
    const x = (time: number) => CHART_LEFT + ((Math.min(Math.max(time, CHART_MIN_MS), CHART_MAX_MS) - CHART_MIN_MS) / (CHART_MAX_MS - CHART_MIN_MS)) * (CHART_RIGHT - CHART_LEFT);

    function draw() {
      const result = simulate({ commitWait: select('wait').value === 'on', epsilonMs: Number(select('uncertainty').value), clockGapMs: Number(select('gap').value), paxosMs: PAXOS_MS });
      const waiting = select('wait').value === 'on';
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = ms(result.writeLatencyMs);
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = waiting && result.commitWaitMs > PAXOS_MS ? 'the commit wait is longer than the Paxos commit, so it sets the time' : waiting ? 'the commit wait is hidden inside the Paxos commit' : 'only the Paxos commit';
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = waiting ? ms(result.commitWaitMs) : 'skipped';
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = waiting ? 'twice the uncertainty' : `it would have been ${ms(result.commitWaitMs)}`;
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = result.orderPreserved ? `after by ${ms(result.marginMs)}` : `BEFORE by ${ms(-result.marginMs)}`;
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = `T1 got ${result.firstTimestampMs}, T2 got ${result.secondTimestampMs}`;
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = result.boundHolds ? 'yes' : 'no';
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = `the clocks differ by ${ms(Number(select('gap').value))}; the bound allows ${ms(result.commitWaitMs)}`;
      const bad = [false, false, !result.orderPreserved, !result.boundHolds];
      ['b1', 'b2', 'b3', 'b4'].forEach((b, i) => q<HTMLElement>(`[data-${b}]`).style.setProperty('--c', bad[i] ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)'));

      const place = (key: string, time: number, dy: number) => {
        q(`[data-${key}]`).setAttribute('cx', x(time).toFixed(1)); q(`[data-${key}]`).setAttribute('cy', String(CHART_Y + dy));
        q(`[data-${key}-label]`).setAttribute('x', x(time).toFixed(1)); q(`[data-${key}-label]`).setAttribute('y', String(CHART_Y + dy - 14 - LABEL_OFFSET));
      };
      place('t1', result.firstTimestampMs, 0); place('t2', result.secondTimestampMs, 0);
      q('[data-chart]').setAttribute('aria-label', `T1's commit timestamp is ${result.firstTimestampMs} ms and T2's is ${result.secondTimestampMs} ms: T2 is ${result.orderPreserved ? 'after' : 'before'} T1`);

      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); const broken = !result.orderPreserved; out.classList.toggle('bad', broken);
      if (broken && !result.boundHolds) out.textContent = `The clocks differ by more than the uncertainty TrueTime claimed, so even the commit wait cannot protect the order: T2 is ${ms(-result.marginMs)} before T1.`;
      else if (broken) out.textContent = `External consistency is broken: T2 started after T1 had committed but was given a timestamp ${ms(-result.marginMs)} earlier. Turn the commit wait on.`;
      else if (waiting && result.commitWaitMs > PAXOS_MS) out.textContent = `The order is right, but each write waited ${ms(result.commitWaitMs)}: while the uncertainty is large, commit wait slows writes down.`;
      else out.textContent = `The order is right: T2 is ${ms(result.marginMs)} after T1.`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      Object.keys(DEFAULTS).forEach((k) => (select(k).value = DEFAULTS[k]));
      draw();
    });
    draw();
  });
</script>
